From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] WinSystemAmlogic: present the frame when the GUI was composited

During fullscreen video with a static GUI the application skips the GUI
render pass, but with HDR GUI compositing on it still draws the frame:
the raw HDR subtitles go onto the back buffer and CompositeGui blends the
cached GUI over them. PresentRender only presented when the GUI pass
itself had drawn, so that work was discarded every frame and the render
loop had nothing to pace it.

Present whenever compositing drew the frame. The GBM backend already flips
whenever a video layer is up.

The frame also has to be complete. The GBM backend clears the back buffer
in EndGuiComposite; the Amlogic one clears it only in ClearBackBuffer, and
only when the GUI will render. A skipped frame therefore drew over whatever
that swap-chain buffer last held: when a subtitle changed or ended, only
the buffer drawn on the next rendered frame was cleared and the others
kept the old subtitle, so it strobed as the buffers rotated. Clear on
every frame that is presented. SDR playback does not composite, does not
present skipped frames, and is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/amlogic/WinSystemAmlogicGLESContext.cpp
@@ -283,7 +283,9 @@
   }
 
   SetVSync(true);
-  if (rendered)
+  // A frame whose GUI render was skipped still wrote the back buffer when
+  // compositing is on, so it has to be presented like any other.
+  if (rendered || (videoLayer && m_guiCompositing))
   {
 #if defined(EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync) && defined(EGL_KHR_fence_sync)
     if (m_eglFence)
@@ -574,7 +576,10 @@
 
 void CWinSystemAmlogicGLESContext::ClearBackBuffer(bool guiWillRender)
 {
-  if (!guiWillRender)
+  // A skipped GUI render is still presented while compositing, and nothing
+  // else clears the back buffer, so it would show the swap chain's stale
+  // content: an ended subtitle strobes across the buffers.
+  if (!guiWillRender && !m_guiCompositing)
     return;
 
   // Clear the backbuffer before video renders. In the FBO compositing path,
